1
00:00:00,959 --> 00:00:03,169
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

2
00:00:03,253 --> 00:00:09,009
["Mr. Tailor" playing]

3
00:00:09,092 --> 00:00:10,760
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

4
00:00:10,844 --> 00:00:12,887
♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i> ♪

5
00:00:12,971 --> 00:00:16,725
♪ <i>One cut, and it's settled</i> ♪

6
00:00:16,808 --> 00:00:19,978
[Mercado] <i>They'll find out</i>
<i>that your identity yesterday was fake.</i>

7
00:00:20,061 --> 00:00:22,147
<i>If that happens,</i>
<i>the embassy will be alerted.</i>

8
00:00:22,230 --> 00:00:26,025
<i>It's either they'll lock down the embassy</i>
<i>or move your target.</i>

9
00:00:26,109 --> 00:00:28,445
So, you must hurry, Atoy.

10
00:00:28,528 --> 00:00:29,362
[in English] Ready to execute.

11
00:00:29,446 --> 00:00:31,072
[in English] My friend, how are you?

12
00:00:31,156 --> 00:00:34,200
[in English] I would want you to meet
my lovely daughter, Audrey.

13
00:00:34,284 --> 00:00:36,578
- [in English] Hello.
- Audrey, Viktor Petrov.

14
00:00:36,661 --> 00:00:38,580
[in English] The ambassador of Zahran.

15
00:00:38,663 --> 00:00:39,706
[in English] Uh, hello, Atoy.

16
00:00:39,789 --> 00:00:43,793
I-I just wanted to let you know
I'm here now at the Embassy of Zahran.

17
00:00:43,877 --> 00:00:45,795
[Atoy] What are you doing here
at the embassy?

18
00:00:45,879 --> 00:00:47,922
I can't face Brother Atoy
because I feel guilty.

19
00:00:48,006 --> 00:00:50,091
But you didn't do anything wrong.

20
00:00:50,175 --> 00:00:51,176
I didn't do anything wrong,

21
00:00:51,259 --> 00:00:53,803
but I'm ashamed
of how you deceived his family.

22
00:00:53,887 --> 00:00:55,597
I'm not so shameless like you.

23
00:00:55,680 --> 00:00:57,348
PREVIOUSLY

24
00:00:57,432 --> 00:00:58,558
[in Russian] You idiot!

25
00:00:59,476 --> 00:01:03,480
[in English] Get off your phone
and get back to work!

26
00:01:03,563 --> 00:01:06,858
[Paldo] <i>Sir Delfin's death anniversary</i>
<i>must be near.</i>

27
00:01:06,941 --> 00:01:09,736
[Cita] Delfin said when you were a child,

28
00:01:09,819 --> 00:01:11,821
you were a good kid,

29
00:01:11,905 --> 00:01:16,493
and he was sure
you'd grow up to be a good man.

30
00:01:16,576 --> 00:01:18,787
[Victor, in English] <i>I thought</i>
<i>you liked the music, Audrey.</i>

31
00:01:18,870 --> 00:01:22,165
- [in English] <i>Why-- Why did you join us?</i>
- [safe keys blipping]

32
00:01:22,248 --> 00:01:24,417
[Audrey, in English] <i>I just</i>
<i>wanna make sure that</i>

33
00:01:24,501 --> 00:01:26,669
<i>my dad doesn't do something silly!</i>

34
00:01:26,753 --> 00:01:30,757
[in English] You have
a very protective daughter, Dmitri.

35
00:01:30,840 --> 00:01:32,509
[Victor chuckles]

36
00:01:32,592 --> 00:01:33,885
[safe blipping]

37
00:01:33,968 --> 00:01:34,969
[door lock clicks]

38
00:01:36,471 --> 00:01:40,391
[rousing music playing]

39
00:01:46,189 --> 00:01:48,358
[in English] Isn't
my daughter sweet? [sighs]

40
00:01:48,441 --> 00:01:50,568
[in English] She's most valuable to me.

41
00:01:50,652 --> 00:01:51,986
[in English] Very protective.

42
00:01:52,070 --> 00:01:53,863
[both chuckle]

43
00:01:53,947 --> 00:01:56,116
[in English] Oh, I like your office.

44
00:01:56,991 --> 00:01:59,285
- [in English] Very nice.
- [in English] My little home.

45
00:01:59,994 --> 00:02:03,248
[in English] Everything
came from, uh, Russia?

46
00:02:03,331 --> 00:02:04,457
[in English] Just about.

47
00:02:05,416 --> 00:02:07,127
[in English] But this, I'm very proud of.

48
00:02:07,210 --> 00:02:10,421
[suspicious music playing]

49
00:02:10,505 --> 00:02:11,673
[Dmitri, in English] Tell me about it.

50
00:02:12,257 --> 00:02:15,426
[Viktor, in English] Uh, this is very old.

51
00:02:15,510 --> 00:02:19,639
[indistinct chattering]

52
00:02:19,722 --> 00:02:22,225
[Viktor, in English]
It's very scary, actually.

53
00:02:22,725 --> 00:02:27,063
[tense music playing]

54
00:02:30,900 --> 00:02:33,778
[in English] Audrey,
what are you doing there?

55
00:02:35,071 --> 00:02:37,615
Um… [chuckles]

56
00:02:37,699 --> 00:02:40,577
[in English] She's probably admiring
my wine collection.

57
00:02:40,660 --> 00:02:41,995
[in English] Oh! [chuckles]

58
00:02:42,078 --> 00:02:43,121
- [in English] But…
- [in English] Yes.

59
00:02:43,204 --> 00:02:46,833
[in English] I want to show
the two of you something very special.

60
00:02:46,916 --> 00:02:48,251
[music fades]

61
00:02:48,334 --> 00:02:51,379
[suave theme music playing]

62
00:02:52,964 --> 00:02:54,799
[motorcycle revving]

63
00:02:54,883 --> 00:02:56,718
[sewing machine whirring]

64
00:02:56,801 --> 00:02:59,262
[scratches]

65
00:02:59,345 --> 00:03:02,599
[sewing machine clacking]

66
00:03:02,682 --> 00:03:04,309
- [gun cocks]
- [gunshots]

67
00:03:04,392 --> 00:03:05,977
[gunshots]

68
00:03:06,060 --> 00:03:08,271
[clacking]

69
00:03:08,354 --> 00:03:10,356
[clicking]

70
00:03:11,399 --> 00:03:13,818
[electronic blipping]

71
00:03:17,614 --> 00:03:19,616
[music fades]

72
00:03:20,658 --> 00:03:23,161
Later, when the shipment arrives,
we must all be complete.

73
00:03:23,244 --> 00:03:25,371
- [in English] Yes, boss.
- It must be protected properly.

74
00:03:26,497 --> 00:03:27,707
You two, at the gate.

75
00:03:27,790 --> 00:03:29,125
Roger.

76
00:03:29,208 --> 00:03:30,460
The rest with me.

77
00:03:30,543 --> 00:03:33,546
[pensive music playing]

78
00:03:37,884 --> 00:03:39,469
What kind of shipment is this?

79
00:03:40,637 --> 00:03:42,263
Why must everyone be there?

80
00:03:43,014 --> 00:03:45,808
We're sending more women this time.

81
00:03:45,892 --> 00:03:47,602
It cannot fail.

82
00:03:48,728 --> 00:03:50,271
Is there a problem, Paldo?

83
00:03:50,772 --> 00:03:54,192
[anxious music playing]

84
00:03:55,193 --> 00:03:56,194
Can I pass?

85
00:03:56,277 --> 00:03:57,278
What?

86
00:03:58,529 --> 00:04:01,157
I don't want to do this anymore.

87
00:04:01,241 --> 00:04:02,325
I'm leaving the group.

88
00:04:02,408 --> 00:04:04,160
Are you crazy?

89
00:04:04,744 --> 00:04:06,496
- [music fades]
- You cannot leave the group!

90
00:04:06,579 --> 00:04:07,580
[Red] Who's leaving?

91
00:04:07,664 --> 00:04:11,000
[tense music playing]

92
00:04:17,548 --> 00:04:21,386
[in English] Is that a… broken car emblem?

93
00:04:21,469 --> 00:04:22,637
[in English] Yes.

94
00:04:22,720 --> 00:04:25,890
[in English] That's from my first car
from my junkyard.

95
00:04:26,391 --> 00:04:28,935
- [in English] You have a junkyard?
- [in Russian] Yes.

96
00:04:30,228 --> 00:04:33,106
[in English] In San Rodolfo, Bulacan.

97
00:04:33,189 --> 00:04:34,148
[sinister music playing]

98
00:04:34,232 --> 00:04:37,110
[in English] I'm thinking of expanding,

99
00:04:37,193 --> 00:04:40,029
but I have a slight problem.

100
00:04:40,530 --> 00:04:43,741
[in English] I'm having
a hard time shipping the cars.

101
00:04:45,076 --> 00:04:49,289
[in English] My friend,
why didn't you tell me?

102
00:04:49,372 --> 00:04:51,624
[in English] I have a shipping business.

103
00:04:52,250 --> 00:04:54,335
[in English] I can definitely
help you with that.

104
00:04:54,419 --> 00:04:56,004
[in English] That is good!

105
00:04:57,171 --> 00:04:59,465
[in English] Come, let's talk.
Please, have a--

106
00:05:03,678 --> 00:05:06,389
[in English] That's not
supposed to be there.

107
00:05:06,472 --> 00:05:07,432
[Dmitri, in English] What do you mean?

108
00:05:08,224 --> 00:05:09,392
[in English] This.

109
00:05:09,475 --> 00:05:10,560
‪[dramatic stinging]

110
00:05:16,816 --> 00:05:17,942
[in English] What the hell?

111
00:05:18,526 --> 00:05:20,445
Why do you have a hole in your window?

112
00:05:20,528 --> 00:05:25,158
[music swells]

113
00:05:25,241 --> 00:05:27,201
[music fades]

114
00:05:27,285 --> 00:05:28,578
Sorry, Boss Red.

115
00:05:31,164 --> 00:05:32,123
You don't want to do this anymore?

116
00:05:33,833 --> 00:05:35,043
You want out?

117
00:05:36,586 --> 00:05:39,380
Won't you regret the large amount of money
you would make today?

118
00:05:40,506 --> 00:05:43,051
Boss, maybe he's richer than us.

119
00:05:43,134 --> 00:05:45,303
Looks like he's bragging already.

120
00:05:45,386 --> 00:05:46,763
[ominous music playing]

121
00:05:46,846 --> 00:05:47,680
Don't tease him.

122
00:05:48,931 --> 00:05:50,725
Paldo wants to change his life.

123
00:05:51,726 --> 00:05:53,269
Why don't we let him?

124
00:05:57,648 --> 00:05:59,734
Don't worry, it's okay.

125
00:06:00,610 --> 00:06:01,986
But we still have something to discuss.

126
00:06:03,654 --> 00:06:05,156
Thank you, boss.

127
00:06:05,239 --> 00:06:06,199
All right.

128
00:06:11,079 --> 00:06:14,040
Boss, you let him go?

129
00:06:14,791 --> 00:06:16,084
[sniffs]

130
00:06:16,167 --> 00:06:18,002
I just gave him a head start.

131
00:06:18,086 --> 00:06:19,212
So, you can enjoy.

132
00:06:19,295 --> 00:06:22,507
[foreboding music playing]

133
00:06:26,302 --> 00:06:27,595
[Mongki, in English] Yes, boss.

134
00:06:27,678 --> 00:06:29,263
[music fades]

135
00:06:29,347 --> 00:06:32,391
[Samir, in English]
I am not a quitter, Ms. Audrey.

136
00:06:33,309 --> 00:06:36,312
[in English] Be ready for Samir. [smirks]

137
00:06:37,605 --> 00:06:39,440
[pensive music playing]

138
00:06:39,524 --> 00:06:41,275
[in English] Excuse me, sir.

139
00:06:41,359 --> 00:06:42,235
[in English] Yes?

140
00:06:42,318 --> 00:06:46,405
[in English] The Sokolov brothers
who attended the summit are impostors.

141
00:06:46,906 --> 00:06:47,782
[in English] Are you sure?

142
00:06:47,865 --> 00:06:49,534
[in English] I am sure, sir.

143
00:06:49,617 --> 00:06:50,827
[in English] I knew it.

144
00:06:51,702 --> 00:06:55,081
[in English] I felt there was
something wrong about this man.

145
00:06:55,164 --> 00:06:56,666
[suspicious music playing]

146
00:06:56,749 --> 00:06:58,292
[in English] We may have a problem.

147
00:07:01,671 --> 00:07:03,464
[in English] We have been compromised.

148
00:07:03,548 --> 00:07:04,841
[in English] Tell the guests
to leave right now.

149
00:07:04,924 --> 00:07:06,050
[in English] Where's the ambassador?

150
00:07:07,635 --> 00:07:08,719
[in English] What's that?

151
00:07:08,803 --> 00:07:10,430
- [music swells]
- [grunts]

152
00:07:10,513 --> 00:07:11,889
[gasps]

153
00:07:11,973 --> 00:07:13,182
Why-- Why did you do that?!

154
00:07:13,266 --> 00:07:14,058
Shh.

155
00:07:14,142 --> 00:07:15,226
[in English] Check every floor.

156
00:07:15,309 --> 00:07:16,644
[in English] I'll go to the ambassador.

157
00:07:16,727 --> 00:07:18,146
[tense music playing]

158
00:07:18,896 --> 00:07:22,525
[gasps]

159
00:07:23,276 --> 00:07:24,235
[in English] Go.

160
00:07:25,069 --> 00:07:26,154
[music fades]

161
00:07:26,237 --> 00:07:30,032
[tense music playing]

162
00:07:30,741 --> 00:07:33,119
[gasps]

163
00:07:42,086 --> 00:07:43,796
[gasping]

164
00:07:43,880 --> 00:07:45,965
[in English] Dad? Help!

165
00:07:46,799 --> 00:07:47,717
[in English] Help!

166
00:07:47,800 --> 00:07:48,843
[in English] Ambassador!

167
00:07:56,684 --> 00:07:57,727
[thuds]

168
00:07:57,810 --> 00:08:00,354
[machine whirring]

169
00:08:00,438 --> 00:08:02,940
[ominous music playing]

170
00:08:03,024 --> 00:08:04,233
[in English] Ambassador!

171
00:08:04,317 --> 00:08:07,570
[tense music playing]

172
00:08:07,653 --> 00:08:08,863
[Audrey, in English] Help, help!

173
00:08:08,946 --> 00:08:10,823
- [in English] Ambassador! Ambassador!
- [Audrey, in English] Help!

174
00:08:10,907 --> 00:08:12,366
- [in English] Help, help my dad.
- Audrey.

175
00:08:12,450 --> 00:08:13,826
[in English] Check on them!
Call the medic!

176
00:08:15,828 --> 00:08:16,662
[Audrey gasps]

177
00:08:16,746 --> 00:08:18,748
[machine clanging]

178
00:08:18,831 --> 00:08:21,834
[tense music playing]

179
00:08:21,918 --> 00:08:23,294
[machine clanging]

180
00:08:35,223 --> 00:08:38,100
[device blipping]

181
00:08:38,184 --> 00:08:42,480
[blipping ends, swoosh]

182
00:08:47,401 --> 00:08:49,362
[in English] Dad. Please help--
Please help him.

183
00:08:49,445 --> 00:08:51,072
[Audrey grunts]

184
00:08:51,155 --> 00:08:51,989
[Audrey, in English] Get him.

185
00:08:52,073 --> 00:08:53,366
[glass screeches]

186
00:08:53,449 --> 00:08:56,035
[device blips]

187
00:08:57,912 --> 00:09:00,164
[music fades]

188
00:09:00,248 --> 00:09:02,959
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

189
00:09:06,879 --> 00:09:08,339
[music fades]

190
00:09:10,925 --> 00:09:12,134
- [radio static]
- [in English] Check on the perimeter.

191
00:09:12,218 --> 00:09:13,427
[in English] We have a breach.

192
00:09:13,511 --> 00:09:15,221
[in English] I repeat,
we have a security breach!

193
00:09:15,304 --> 00:09:16,556
- [in English] Check the perimeter!
- [Audrey, indistinct]

194
00:09:16,639 --> 00:09:18,641
[pensive music playing]

195
00:09:19,267 --> 00:09:21,143
[Audrey mutters]

196
00:09:21,227 --> 00:09:22,520
- [in English] You…
- [Audrey, in English] Wake up.

197
00:09:23,437 --> 00:09:25,022
[in English] What happened here?

198
00:09:25,106 --> 00:09:27,567
[unsettling music playing]

199
00:09:27,650 --> 00:09:29,902
[in English] Uh, s-s-some--
Some guy in a mask

200
00:09:29,986 --> 00:09:31,904
jumped over the kitchen counter.

201
00:09:32,780 --> 00:09:36,576
He ran and hit my dad
and the ambassador over the head and…

202
00:09:36,659 --> 00:09:38,494
he climbed out the hole in the window.

203
00:09:39,537 --> 00:09:42,456
[in English] But you're okay, Ms. Audrey.

204
00:09:44,166 --> 00:09:45,710
[in English] You didn't call for help.

205
00:09:46,586 --> 00:09:49,338
[in English] You didn't scream.
Nothing, you did nothing.

206
00:09:51,340 --> 00:09:53,009
- [music fades]
- [in English] I was in shock.

207
00:09:54,427 --> 00:09:55,303
[in English] And he was holding a gun.

208
00:09:55,386 --> 00:09:56,554
[suspicious music playing]

209
00:09:56,637 --> 00:09:58,180
[in English] He told me not to scream.

210
00:09:58,681 --> 00:10:00,308
[in English] Why didn't he hurt you?

211
00:10:01,392 --> 00:10:02,435
[in English] I don't know!

212
00:10:02,518 --> 00:10:04,228
[in English] Why are you asking me
so many questions?

213
00:10:04,312 --> 00:10:06,939
[in English] Shouldn't you be more worried
about the ambassador and my dad?!

214
00:10:07,023 --> 00:10:09,692
[tense music playing]

215
00:10:09,775 --> 00:10:10,818
[in Russian] I’m not sure.

216
00:10:13,654 --> 00:10:15,531
[in English] Bring her
to the interrogation room.

217
00:10:15,615 --> 00:10:17,783
[rousing music playing]

218
00:10:17,867 --> 00:10:18,993
[in English] Now!

219
00:10:19,076 --> 00:10:20,286
[tense music playing]

220
00:10:20,369 --> 00:10:22,163
[in English] Where are you taking me?
What about my dad?!

221
00:10:22,246 --> 00:10:23,998
[in English] Let go of me!

222
00:10:25,499 --> 00:10:26,959
[in English] Where are we going?!

223
00:10:27,043 --> 00:10:28,794
[music swells]

224
00:10:30,630 --> 00:10:31,589
[music fades]

225
00:10:33,758 --> 00:10:37,136
[mid-tempo rock music playing]

226
00:10:52,902 --> 00:10:54,445
[music fades]

227
00:10:54,528 --> 00:10:55,613
[Atoy] Emerson.

228
00:10:56,572 --> 00:11:01,911
[mid-tempo rock music playing]

229
00:11:07,375 --> 00:11:09,585
[music fades]

230
00:11:10,086 --> 00:11:15,216
[in English] Mr. Ambassador,
we found you on the floor, unconscious.

231
00:11:15,299 --> 00:11:18,552
[in English] Do you remember anything
that happened to you?

232
00:11:18,636 --> 00:11:21,597
[suspicious music playing]

233
00:11:21,680 --> 00:11:22,640
[in English] Wait.

234
00:11:32,942 --> 00:11:36,612
[device blipping]

235
00:11:40,074 --> 00:11:41,409
[tense music playing]

236
00:11:41,492 --> 00:11:42,827
[in English] It's gone!

237
00:11:42,910 --> 00:11:45,287
[in English] It's not here!

238
00:11:45,371 --> 00:11:48,499
[in English] Samir, alert everybody!

239
00:11:49,417 --> 00:11:50,668
[in English] Hold him!

240
00:11:52,586 --> 00:11:55,840
[in English] An important
piece of information is gone!

241
00:11:55,923 --> 00:11:57,842
[in English] Did you
have something to do with this?!

242
00:11:57,925 --> 00:12:00,803
[in English] No! No, Viktor. No!

243
00:12:01,512 --> 00:12:03,639
[in English] I was struck in the head.
I was out cold!

244
00:12:04,723 --> 00:12:06,350
[in English] I-- I don't know this man.

245
00:12:06,434 --> 00:12:07,685
[in English] I swear!

246
00:12:10,062 --> 00:12:11,230
[in English] Where's my daughter?

247
00:12:11,313 --> 00:12:12,481
[in English] She was here. Wh-Where's--

248
00:12:12,565 --> 00:12:15,025
[in English] She's with me
in another room.

249
00:12:15,109 --> 00:12:15,985
[in English] I have her.

250
00:12:16,068 --> 00:12:17,027
Samir.

251
00:12:17,111 --> 00:12:19,363
[in English] Did you catch the thief?

252
00:12:20,239 --> 00:12:21,240
[in English] No.

253
00:12:22,283 --> 00:12:25,119
[in English] I did not. He got away.

254
00:12:25,703 --> 00:12:27,746
[in English] Who could have done this?

255
00:12:28,247 --> 00:12:32,543
[in English] Someone must have helped him.

256
00:12:34,253 --> 00:12:35,212
Viktor.

257
00:12:36,922 --> 00:12:38,883
[in English] I value our friendship!

258
00:12:39,508 --> 00:12:42,678
[in English] I will never
steal anything from you.

259
00:12:42,761 --> 00:12:47,057
[in English] If you want,
I can help you find this man.

260
00:12:47,141 --> 00:12:51,187
[in English] I know
a very good tracker, a man-hunter.

261
00:12:51,270 --> 00:12:55,691
[tense music playing]

262
00:12:56,859 --> 00:12:58,402
[Paldo] Where's the crew hanging out?

263
00:12:58,486 --> 00:12:59,904
- [music concludes]
- Call them. I'll buy drinks!

264
00:13:00,488 --> 00:13:01,280
Hurry.

265
00:13:01,363 --> 00:13:03,365
Ma'am, can I buy soft drinks?

266
00:13:04,533 --> 00:13:06,994
[friend on the phone] <i>Oh? I thought</i>
<i>you had work with Mongki.</i>

267
00:13:07,077 --> 00:13:08,496
[pensive music playing]

268
00:13:08,579 --> 00:13:09,413
Not anymore.

269
00:13:09,497 --> 00:13:10,956
I quit.

270
00:13:11,916 --> 00:13:14,001
I can't take what they're doing anymore.

271
00:13:14,877 --> 00:13:18,923
[tense music playing]

272
00:13:22,885 --> 00:13:24,345
[friend on the phone]
<i>They just let you go like that?</i>

273
00:13:25,804 --> 00:13:28,474
<i>Paldo, be careful.</i>

274
00:13:29,892 --> 00:13:30,768
Why?

275
00:13:31,852 --> 00:13:33,562
I'm still alive, aren't I?

276
00:13:33,646 --> 00:13:35,940
[music swells]

277
00:13:36,023 --> 00:13:41,028
[ominous music playing]

278
00:13:45,199 --> 00:13:49,245
[exhilarating rock music playing]

279
00:13:53,832 --> 00:13:55,501
[Emerson] Sir Ben?

280
00:13:55,584 --> 00:13:56,794
Sir Ben!

281
00:13:56,877 --> 00:13:57,962
[music fades]

282
00:13:58,045 --> 00:13:59,129
Sir Ben, what happened?

283
00:13:59,213 --> 00:14:00,631
I just went to the bathroom!

284
00:14:00,714 --> 00:14:02,925
- [suspicious music playing]
- Why did you leave me right away? Doc!

285
00:14:03,008 --> 00:14:04,260
Wha-- What happened?

286
00:14:04,343 --> 00:14:06,220
Sir Ben, I'm sorry! Sir Ben!

287
00:14:06,303 --> 00:14:08,347
I'm sorry, if you have kids,

288
00:14:08,430 --> 00:14:11,267
I'll pay their tuition. Just live!

289
00:14:11,350 --> 00:14:12,893
Sir Ben! Sir Ben!

290
00:14:12,977 --> 00:14:14,186
Doc! Doc!

291
00:14:14,853 --> 00:14:16,188
What did he die of?

292
00:14:17,022 --> 00:14:18,607
Patient Reyes had cardiac arrest.

293
00:14:18,691 --> 00:14:19,483
[in English] Cardiac arrest?!

294
00:14:19,567 --> 00:14:21,110
[sobs]

295
00:14:21,193 --> 00:14:23,737
But your companion is still alive.

296
00:14:23,821 --> 00:14:25,447
- I just transferred him to the other side.
- Huh?

297
00:14:25,531 --> 00:14:26,699
Who is this?

298
00:14:26,782 --> 00:14:28,450
- [gasps]
- [sneaky music playing]

299
00:14:29,118 --> 00:14:30,578
Doc, what's going on?

300
00:14:31,495 --> 00:14:32,538
Sir Ben!

301
00:14:33,622 --> 00:14:34,540
Doc!

302
00:14:35,249 --> 00:14:36,667
Why didn't you say so?

303
00:14:36,750 --> 00:14:38,586
You're unbelievable.

304
00:14:38,669 --> 00:14:41,797
I was promising scholarships
to someone else.

305
00:14:41,881 --> 00:14:43,591
[chuckles] Sir Ben.

306
00:14:43,674 --> 00:14:45,551
[doctor] Mr. Laput is fine now.

307
00:14:45,634 --> 00:14:47,761
He just fainted because he's anemic.

308
00:14:47,845 --> 00:14:49,680
But I prescribed something for him.

309
00:14:49,763 --> 00:14:51,849
[sighs]

310
00:14:51,932 --> 00:14:53,058
Jesus!

311
00:14:53,142 --> 00:14:54,435
Just anemia?

312
00:14:55,436 --> 00:14:57,021
- [sighs]
- [sneaky music playing]

313
00:14:57,104 --> 00:14:59,106
Thank you. Thank you, Doc.

314
00:14:59,189 --> 00:15:00,816
My God.

315
00:15:00,900 --> 00:15:03,527
Good thing you're okay, Sir Ben.

316
00:15:03,611 --> 00:15:05,237
[Emerson sighs loudly]

317
00:15:05,321 --> 00:15:07,197
I thought something worse happened.

318
00:15:08,198 --> 00:15:09,825
Wait, wait.

319
00:15:09,909 --> 00:15:11,285
- [music concludes]
- Gosh.

320
00:15:11,368 --> 00:15:12,369
[sighs]

321
00:15:12,453 --> 00:15:15,831
[phone ringing]

322
00:15:16,957 --> 00:15:17,791
[in English] Hello?

323
00:15:17,875 --> 00:15:19,251
Hello, Emerson! What's up?

324
00:15:19,335 --> 00:15:20,586
[Emerson on the phone] <i>Atoy, jeez!</i>

325
00:15:21,462 --> 00:15:24,048
Thank God. Sir Ben is okay now.

326
00:15:24,715 --> 00:15:27,968
I didn't know this mission
would be this hard.

327
00:15:28,052 --> 00:15:29,678
- [pensive music playing]
- I'll get back to you, okay?

328
00:15:29,762 --> 00:15:32,181
I hope you got what you needed.

329
00:15:32,264 --> 00:15:34,016
[Atoy on the phone]
<i>Don't-- Don't come back.</i>

330
00:15:34,099 --> 00:15:36,268
<i>It's probably chaotic there!</i>

331
00:15:36,352 --> 00:15:38,312
<i>Go straight to the tailoring shop.</i>

332
00:15:38,395 --> 00:15:40,105
<i>Take care of my car, okay?</i>

333
00:15:40,189 --> 00:15:41,398
Okay. Okay, okay.

334
00:15:41,482 --> 00:15:42,816
[exhales]

335
00:15:42,900 --> 00:15:44,985
[rousing music playing]

336
00:15:46,278 --> 00:15:51,533
[tense music playing]

337
00:15:54,870 --> 00:15:56,497
He's just around.

338
00:15:59,208 --> 00:16:00,668
Surround him!

339
00:16:05,965 --> 00:16:07,299
[music fades]

340
00:16:07,383 --> 00:16:11,720
[ominous music playing]

341
00:16:13,639 --> 00:16:14,723
[Mongki] Look over there.

342
00:16:16,725 --> 00:16:18,519
- [grunting]
- [thumping]

343
00:16:18,602 --> 00:16:20,479
[groaning and grunting]

344
00:16:20,562 --> 00:16:23,232
[thumping]

345
00:16:23,315 --> 00:16:28,445
[grunting and groaning]

346
00:16:30,739 --> 00:16:32,783
[upbeat rock music playing]

347
00:16:33,951 --> 00:16:35,202
[thumps, then thuds]

348
00:16:35,285 --> 00:16:37,913
[Mongki] Chase him! Stand up!

349
00:16:39,832 --> 00:16:41,959
[music fades]

350
00:16:47,506 --> 00:16:49,967
[line rings]

351
00:16:50,050 --> 00:16:53,345
[panting, in English] Sir. Bingo.
I got the package.

352
00:16:53,429 --> 00:16:56,015
[Mercado, in English] <i>Move to my location</i>
<i>immediately for turnover.</i>

353
00:16:56,098 --> 00:16:58,100
- [in English] Copy.
- [Mercado, in English] <i>Good job, Padua.</i>

354
00:16:58,183 --> 00:17:00,269
[in English] Oh, okay. To the rally point.

355
00:17:00,352 --> 00:17:02,062
[in English] Okay.
I'll meet you there now, sir.

356
00:17:02,146 --> 00:17:03,147
[in English] Okay. Thank you.

357
00:17:03,230 --> 00:17:04,273
[tense music playing]

358
00:17:04,356 --> 00:17:06,358
[phone rings]

359
00:17:07,526 --> 00:17:09,153
Hello, Miss Cita!

360
00:17:09,236 --> 00:17:10,446
Why did you call?

361
00:17:11,030 --> 00:17:13,407
Emerson, how's your mission?

362
00:17:13,490 --> 00:17:15,242
I can't contact Atoy.

363
00:17:15,325 --> 00:17:17,578
Ah, he's busy, busy.

364
00:17:17,661 --> 00:17:18,579
You won't be able to talk to him.

365
00:17:18,662 --> 00:17:20,289
Weren't you together?

366
00:17:20,372 --> 00:17:25,252
Since I dropped him off,
I haven't seen him.

367
00:17:25,335 --> 00:17:27,379
He told me to go home.

368
00:17:27,463 --> 00:17:29,339
I didn't even feel like

369
00:17:29,423 --> 00:17:30,883
I was in dangerous missions.

370
00:17:30,966 --> 00:17:35,304
He just sent me with an anemic patient
to the hospital, and that was it.

371
00:17:35,387 --> 00:17:37,639
- [quirky music playing]
- So, what do you want to happen?

372
00:17:37,723 --> 00:17:39,808
Miss, of course.

373
00:17:39,892 --> 00:17:43,145
I want it like in action movies.

374
00:17:43,228 --> 00:17:48,525
The ones I see online,
with adrenaline rushes.

375
00:17:48,609 --> 00:17:50,319
This Atoy, the way he sells it to me,

376
00:17:50,402 --> 00:17:52,446
you'd think it was such
an important mission.

377
00:17:52,529 --> 00:17:55,866
He said it was for the country.

378
00:17:55,949 --> 00:17:58,243
But it didn't feel that way to me.

379
00:17:58,327 --> 00:18:00,287
Oh, Emerson.

380
00:18:00,370 --> 00:18:02,039
At least you're safe!

381
00:18:02,122 --> 00:18:06,877
Just wait. That adrenaline rush
you're looking for will come.

382
00:18:06,960 --> 00:18:08,545
Okay. Take care.

383
00:18:08,629 --> 00:18:10,255
Yes, all right.

384
00:18:12,257 --> 00:18:13,258
[T-Bak] Pass right away!

385
00:18:14,718 --> 00:18:16,845
Hey, Gavin! Wait.

386
00:18:16,929 --> 00:18:19,014
[T-Bak, in English] Gavin, my man!

387
00:18:19,098 --> 00:18:20,849
[in English] Long time no see!

388
00:18:21,683 --> 00:18:22,851
- [light music playing]
- [T-Bak] How are you?

389
00:18:22,935 --> 00:18:24,478
[Billy] Busy with his girlfriend.

390
00:18:24,978 --> 00:18:26,605
Karla isn't with you?

391
00:18:26,688 --> 00:18:27,773
[Putoy] I don't know.

392
00:18:27,856 --> 00:18:30,567
She suddenly got mad at us
just because of iced water.

393
00:18:30,651 --> 00:18:33,987
Yes, and we're heading to FO now!

394
00:18:34,071 --> 00:18:35,697
She doesn't show up here anymore!

395
00:18:36,365 --> 00:18:37,991
Let her be!

396
00:18:38,075 --> 00:18:40,536
You've been friends for so long,
and you fight over iced water?

397
00:18:40,619 --> 00:18:42,162
She didn't say anything.

398
00:18:42,246 --> 00:18:43,330
What, are we supposed to guess?

399
00:18:44,039 --> 00:18:45,249
Just understand her.

400
00:18:45,999 --> 00:18:47,042
[phone vibrates]

401
00:18:47,126 --> 00:18:48,168
[in English] Babe?

402
00:18:48,252 --> 00:18:49,503
Yes, we're on later.

403
00:18:50,295 --> 00:18:51,255
I'll pick you up.

404
00:18:51,338 --> 00:18:53,006
[in English] All right. See you.

405
00:18:55,551 --> 00:18:57,219
[music stops]

406
00:18:58,595 --> 00:19:01,306
[bright music playing]

407
00:19:01,390 --> 00:19:02,516
Karla?

408
00:19:05,435 --> 00:19:06,979
- [Putoy] Did you see her?
- [T-Bak] No, nothing.

409
00:19:08,147 --> 00:19:09,439
I'll go ahead, bros.

410
00:19:09,523 --> 00:19:10,440
- [Gavin] See you.
- Take care!

411
00:19:19,491 --> 00:19:21,076
[in English] Dad? Dad!

412
00:19:21,160 --> 00:19:22,244
[Dmitri, in English] Yes.

413
00:19:22,327 --> 00:19:24,663
- [in English] Are you okay? [sighs]
- [in English] I'm fine.

414
00:19:24,746 --> 00:19:26,790
You, were you hurt by the thief?

415
00:19:26,874 --> 00:19:28,584
[in English] No, no.

416
00:19:28,667 --> 00:19:31,461
[in English] But do they have
any leads who did it?

417
00:19:31,545 --> 00:19:32,379
[Dmitri sighs]

418
00:19:32,462 --> 00:19:33,755
None.

419
00:19:34,256 --> 00:19:35,757
[in English] But can you imagine?

420
00:19:36,466 --> 00:19:42,389
He made a hole in the window,
entered and exited from the ninth floor.

421
00:19:42,472 --> 00:19:45,559
[in English] To go through that effort,
it must be a highly skilled thief.

422
00:19:45,642 --> 00:19:48,145
- [suspicious music playing]
- [Dmitri scoffs]

423
00:19:48,228 --> 00:19:51,190
They even suspected me, as an accomplice.

424
00:19:51,273 --> 00:19:53,317
So, they held me in the office.

425
00:19:54,568 --> 00:19:57,863
I want to help them catch the thief.

426
00:19:58,572 --> 00:20:02,534
There's national data on the laptop
that was stolen.

427
00:20:04,244 --> 00:20:06,496
[in English] Dad,
it's none of our business.

428
00:20:06,580 --> 00:20:10,667
And besides, there's nothing
you can do about it anyway.

429
00:20:11,293 --> 00:20:12,127
[sighs]

430
00:20:12,211 --> 00:20:16,006
I just thought,
maybe Atoy could help us.

431
00:20:16,089 --> 00:20:17,716
[in English] Since he's a tracker.

432
00:20:17,799 --> 00:20:19,176
[sighs]

433
00:20:20,093 --> 00:20:22,971
After you told him to stay away from me?

434
00:20:23,931 --> 00:20:26,141
[in English] I don't think so, Dad.

435
00:20:26,225 --> 00:20:31,939
[music swells]

436
00:20:33,315 --> 00:20:35,192
[music fades]

437
00:20:37,986 --> 00:20:43,575
[mid-tempo rock music playing]

438
00:20:45,244 --> 00:20:46,578
- [in English] Boss.
- Oh?

439
00:20:46,662 --> 00:20:48,497
Can I borrow your motorbike?

440
00:20:48,580 --> 00:20:49,414
Borrow my motorbike?

441
00:20:49,498 --> 00:20:50,624
Are you crazy?

442
00:20:50,707 --> 00:20:51,833
[grunts]

443
00:20:55,003 --> 00:20:55,837
[Atoy] Sorry, bro.

444
00:20:55,921 --> 00:20:57,714
[in English] Matter of national security.

445
00:21:06,139 --> 00:21:07,641
Can I borrow the helmet too?

446
00:21:10,227 --> 00:21:14,564
[ominous music playing]

447
00:21:18,026 --> 00:21:19,152
Boss, there!

448
00:21:19,236 --> 00:21:20,988
- He passed here!
- Follow him, quick!

449
00:21:21,071 --> 00:21:24,574
[upbeat rock music playing]

450
00:21:30,163 --> 00:21:32,499
[music swells]

451
00:21:38,297 --> 00:21:39,506
[tense music playing]

452
00:21:39,589 --> 00:21:41,675
- Paldo.
- [panting]

453
00:21:41,758 --> 00:21:42,968
Paldo, what happened to you?

454
00:21:43,051 --> 00:21:45,220
Emerson, help me. Someone's chasing me.

455
00:21:45,304 --> 00:21:47,889
- Why? What happened to you?
- Help me.

456
00:21:47,973 --> 00:21:52,519
[engine running]

457
00:21:53,186 --> 00:21:55,897
[panting]

458
00:21:56,481 --> 00:21:57,316
[Mongki] Where did he go?!

459
00:21:57,399 --> 00:21:59,484
- Point it out! Where?!
- [gasps]

460
00:22:00,485 --> 00:22:02,487
[gasping]

461
00:22:04,573 --> 00:22:06,116
Wait. Did you rob someone?!

462
00:22:06,199 --> 00:22:07,534
Don't make this a getaway car!

463
00:22:07,617 --> 00:22:08,493
This is Atoy's car!

464
00:22:09,119 --> 00:22:11,079
Someone's going to kill me, Emerson!
Do you understand?!

465
00:22:11,163 --> 00:22:13,415
- Who?
- There! Them!

466
00:22:13,498 --> 00:22:15,083
- [sharp exhale]
- [tense music playing]

467
00:22:15,167 --> 00:22:16,001
Paldo!

468
00:22:17,377 --> 00:22:19,004
[Mongki] You exhausted us!

469
00:22:19,087 --> 00:22:20,547
They're going to kill me!

470
00:22:20,630 --> 00:22:22,341
I know them. That's Red's crew!

471
00:22:22,424 --> 00:22:27,179
Get down from there,
or we'll rain bullets on you!

472
00:22:27,262 --> 00:22:28,305
Paldo, jeez!

473
00:22:28,388 --> 00:22:30,724
Why did you drag me into this?!

474
00:22:30,807 --> 00:22:31,975
I don't want trouble!

475
00:22:32,059 --> 00:22:34,019
I don't want an adrenaline rush.
I'm not a hero!

476
00:22:34,102 --> 00:22:36,271
[Mongki] One, two!

477
00:22:36,354 --> 00:22:37,773
[in English] Atoy, what would you do?!

478
00:22:37,856 --> 00:22:40,150
Two and a half!

479
00:22:40,233 --> 00:22:41,234
Possess me, Atoy!

480
00:22:41,318 --> 00:22:42,694
Okay, I'll just get out
so you won't get involved!

481
00:22:42,778 --> 00:22:44,196
No, no, no, no, no.
Wait, wait, wait, wait, wait!

482
00:22:44,279 --> 00:22:46,490
I'll handle it. I'll save you.
Put on your seat belt!

483
00:22:46,573 --> 00:22:47,699
Put on your seat belt, then duck!

484
00:22:47,783 --> 00:22:49,367
Duck!

485
00:22:49,451 --> 00:22:51,244
- [grunts]
- [rock music playing]

486
00:22:54,372 --> 00:22:56,166
[screams]

487
00:23:01,129 --> 00:23:03,423
- [laughing]
- Faster! Faster!

488
00:23:03,507 --> 00:23:05,550
- Whoo!
- [growls]

489
00:23:05,634 --> 00:23:08,303
[music swells]

490
00:23:08,386 --> 00:23:10,722
[music fades]

491
00:23:10,806 --> 00:23:13,975
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

492
00:23:14,059 --> 00:23:18,355
["Mr. Tailor" playing]

493
00:23:18,939 --> 00:23:20,607
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

494
00:23:20,690 --> 00:23:22,567
♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i> ♪

495
00:23:22,651 --> 00:23:25,946
♪ <i>One cut, and it's settled</i> ♪

496
00:23:26,029 --> 00:23:30,492
♪ <i>In the tangle of the city</i>
<i>You're the timing</i> ♪

497
00:23:30,575 --> 00:23:33,912
♪ <i>When you cut…</i> ♪

498
00:23:33,995 --> 00:23:34,955
[Atoy, in English] Sir.

499
00:23:35,038 --> 00:23:37,874
♪ <i>Like a bubble, like a bubble</i>
<i>Like a bubble</i> ♪

500
00:23:37,958 --> 00:23:40,252
♪ <i>When the cutter knows how to hit</i> ♪

501
00:23:47,342 --> 00:23:48,844
[music swells]

502
00:23:48,927 --> 00:23:53,140
[electronic blipping]

503
00:23:53,223 --> 00:23:57,561
[tense music playing]

504
00:23:57,644 --> 00:23:58,854
[gunshots]

505
00:23:58,937 --> 00:24:00,230
[gasps] They're here!

506
00:24:00,313 --> 00:24:01,398
Leave now. Let me handle this!

507
00:24:01,481 --> 00:24:02,315
No, no!

508
00:24:02,399 --> 00:24:04,401
[Emerson] We're both getting out of here!

509
00:24:04,484 --> 00:24:05,443
[Emerson grunts]

510
00:24:05,527 --> 00:24:06,945
Emerson, you must survive!

511
00:24:07,028 --> 00:24:08,780
You need to tell Atoy the truth!

512
00:24:08,864 --> 00:24:11,199
[Atoy] <i>So, he already knew!</i>
<i>Why is he only telling me now?</i>

513
00:24:11,283 --> 00:24:13,410
I understand. Okay, okay.
Let out all your anger.

514
00:24:13,493 --> 00:24:16,580
But remember, you're not a killer.

515
00:24:16,663 --> 00:24:19,541
There's no legal way for demons like him!

516
00:24:19,624 --> 00:24:20,876
UP NEXT

517
00:24:21,459 --> 00:24:24,963
[T-Bak] There are men
outside Paldo's house!

518
00:24:25,046 --> 00:24:27,048
And they're shooting at his house!

519
00:24:27,132 --> 00:24:28,425
It's Mongki's crew.

520
00:24:28,508 --> 00:24:31,219
- Maybe Red is with them. Move!
- [Emerson] 'Toy, 'Toy, 'Toy, 'Toy, 'Toy!

521
00:24:31,303 --> 00:24:32,804
- Think about this first, Atoy--
- [Munggo] Atoy.

522
00:24:32,888 --> 00:24:34,014
It's Ibyang!

523
00:24:34,097 --> 00:24:35,432
[Munggo] She was taken to the hospital!

524
00:24:35,974 --> 00:24:39,394
♪ <i>One cut, and it's settled</i> ♪

525
00:24:39,477 --> 00:24:41,813
♪ <i>Fix it</i> ♪

526
00:24:41,897 --> 00:24:42,939
Subtitle translation by: Rachel C. Arias
